user
Round 3 (delta-only) review of the Concrete slice-0 branch, after the first macOS run of the AArch64 stack analysis (scripts/checks/lib/stack_bound.py) refused all real Mach-O code. The diff below (9ed1e1cff..397d7811):
(a) the Mach-O __stubs section is one unnamed symbol, so the gate appends `stub ADDR SYMBOL` lines parsed from `llvm-objdump --macho --indirect-symbols` (only the (__TEXT,__stubs) block), and a call is external only when its target address is exactly a stub entry (ELF: a PLT symbol name, `NAME@plt`, as before);
(b) LCB saves/restores the link register with a single `str x30, [sp, #k]` / `ldr x30, [sp, #k]`: an exact 8-byte store of x30 (or x29) to an sp/x29-based slot becomes a saved slot tagged with the register's current state, and a load of x30/x29 is allowed only from an exact slot with the same tag (restoring that state); any other x30 load is still refused;
(c) the link-register flag left the join equality key: joins take the conjunction (a call inside a loop made it differ at the loop head), and every return still requires lr valid;
(d) the uncapped artifacts gate raises an inherited soft address-space cap to the hard limit, or fails (exit 2);
(e) each analysed disassembly is kept in the report.
CI results at 2ea89cab: real code accepted on both platforms; macOS LLDB measurements within bound (e.g. LLVM bound 96 measured 48-96; LCB bound 144 measured 112-144); only two controls failed, fixed in 397d7811. Two real macOS disassemblies are attached as files answer.lcb.aarch64-macos.dis and answer.llvm.aarch64-macos.dis (Codex/Kimi can read them).
Soundness claim: for code the analysis accepts, under the module docstring's premises, the bound covers every stack byte addressed. Find accepted inputs that break it (an understated bound or an unbounded resource), especially through (b) and (c): e.g. a slot reread, an x30 restored from a stale slot, a return with a wrong lr, a stub address spoof. Findings with file:line and a concrete accepted reproducer; mark each real defect or preference. End with exactly one line: VERDICT: ACCEPT, VERDICT: ACCEPT-WITH-CHANGES or VERDICT: REJECT. The diff is ./DELTA.diff. Do not modify files.
